d":"IC_kwDOAAjKyc47ue7k","user":{"login":"Mugen87","id":12612165,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNjEyMTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12612165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87","html_url":"https://github.com/Mugen87","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mugen87/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-12-28T11:33:09Z","updated_at":"2021-12-28T11:41:18Z","body":"Here is a minified live example that demonstrates the issue: https://jsfiddle.net/sgL6obhz/1/\r\n\r\nYour findings made it much easier to finally reproduce this issue in a small test case. The idea is to create two keyframe tracks animating the same property (e.g. `Object3D.position`) and then create for each track a clip. Uncaching a mesh while both animations are playbacked produces the issue. After some debugging, I'm sure this is the same root cause for #22036.\r\n\r\n A missing statement in `AnimationMixer._bindAction()` produces a wrong reference count which potentially breaks `_removeInactiveBindingsForAction()`. It breaks because multiple actions share the same `PropertyMixer` (binding) but the code did not account for this particular use case and thus did not raise the reference count. Your PR fixes the issue.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/1002041060/reacti